For a live connection the project file and system root folder typically is a subfolder in the Omniverse
Nucleus project folder that is managed by the Omniverse Nucleus server.
Compare the examples for both use cases below.
Create and Activate a Live Connection or a Filesystem Connection
Specify these instructions to create and activate a Filesystem Connection with MVA_WriteUSD:
var system_root_path:string = "D:/USD_DataFiles/My_Project01/Library"
var output_path:string = "file://d:/USD_DataFiles/My_Project01A/
myExport.usd"
MVA_writeUSD(output_path+"?sysroot="+system_root_path)
Terminate an Open Live Connection or a Filesystem Connection
Type an empty string to terminate an open Live Connection or an open Filesystem Connection with
MVA_WriteUSD:
MVA_writeUSD("")
Note
Make sure, that Omniverse Composer does not have an open connection to a previously exported
simulation while starting an new export from Plant Simulation with the same project file and system
root.
Note
For a Nucleus Live Connection we do not yet support the function MVA_writeUSD().
