Animating the Simulation Model
Animate the Simulation Model
One of your tasks when creating your simulation model will be to visually show the flow of materials
through the plant you are modeling.
Plant Simulation shows the settings for the animation in 3D on the Tab MU Animation in the dialog Edit
3D Properties.
Activating and Deactivating the Animation
During the simulation run the animation shows the state of the objects and the position and the
movements of the MUs in your simulation model.
Note
As the animation of the parts and of the icons of the object slows down the simulation, only activate it,
when you actually want to show the simulation model to somebody or if you want to check if the model
behaves correctly. For your overnight batch runs we recommend to deactivate it.
You can activate or deactivate MU and State Animation only together, not individually.
• When you activate MUs and States 
 , you immediately see the flow of the parts and the blocked
stations, where the MUs pile up.
• When you deactivate MUs and States while an object intends to change its state, Plant Simulation
delays its display on screen until you activate the animation again or until the object is selected.
To deactivate MUs and States, click 
  on the Home ribbon tab.
To run the simulation with the setting you selected, click Start/Stop Simulation in the EventController.
Note
Clicking 
  on the Home ribbon tab activates MU and State Animation. To start the
simulation without animating objects and MUs, click 
 .
