Make Areas of an Icon Transparent
You can make a contiguous area of a graphics file, which you opened, transparent, so that the background
color of the Frame shines through.
Proceed as follows:
• Open the Icon Editor by clicking Edit Icons on the Home ribbon tab.
• Click 
  or 
  to navigate to the icon you want to make transparent.
• Click the color picker 
  and click in the background of the icon. This makes that color the active
drawing color, which we want to replace.
• Select the transparency color that replaces the active drawing color in the Color Palette proper, not in
the transparency color field!
Make Areas of an Icon Transparent
